92a0476398bef71e0431bccee50cb467b3cb9658a384b700c4d110c032ee6cec[{"version":1,"source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-093347","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-10","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001533615","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1533615/000110465926093347/xrn-20260630x10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/94b4aa63358a5e030610d33f5a1eef5d48ba22881a1ddd3ede1d8a9f3ed88baf.bin","sha256":"94b4aa63358a5e030610d33f5a1eef5d48ba22881a1ddd3ede1d8a9f3ed88baf"},"layers":{"businessProfile":{"status":"evidence_available","evidence":[{"id":"7508632d42c0607aaae22d750d1cde83f0edec56e56ceef71d60c84999a35c45","quote":"We have expanded our business strategy to focus primarily on investments in seniors housing communities that provide an attractive rate of return relative to our cost of capital and are in attractive markets with favorable demographic trends. We believe these asset classes are well positioned to benefit from the growing needs of an aging population and support our goals of providing stockholders with (i) attractive dividends and (ii) stock price appreciation. We are focused on transitioning our asset base from one historically concentrated in outpatient medical facilities to one more heavily weighted toward seniors housing communities.","context":"Business Overview and Strategy","section":"Business Overview and Strategy","block":447,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-093347","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-10","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001533615","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1533615/000110465926093347/xrn-20260630x10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/94b4aa63358a5e030610d33f5a1eef5d48ba22881a1ddd3ede1d8a9f3ed88baf.bin","sha256":"94b4aa63358a5e030610d33f5a1eef5d48ba22881a1ddd3ede1d8a9f3ed88baf"}},{"id":"60bb40949fe7f5599dbd73c433d5f5786014dbea8ab1f330e735ff5b8ea1f6ad","quote":"We also intend to utilize our experience and knowledge of inpatient rehabilitation facilities and outpatient medical real estate to manage our existing joint ventures and to evaluate healthcare real estate opportunities that complement our seniors housing strategy.","context":"We have expanded our business strategy to focus primarily on investments in seniors housing communities that provide an attractive rate of return relative to our cost of capital and are in attractive markets with favorable demographic trends. We believe these asset classes are well positioned to benefit from the growing needs of an aging population and support our goals of providing stockholders with (i) attractive dividends and (ii) stock price appreciation. We are focused on transitioning our asset base from one historically concentrated in outpatient medical facilities to one more heavily weighted toward seniors housing communities.","section":"Business Overview and Strategy","block":448,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-093347","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-10","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001533615","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1533615/000110465926093347/xrn-20260630x10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/94b4aa63358a5e030610d33f5a1eef5d48ba22881a1ddd3ede1d8a9f3ed88baf.bin","sha256":"94b4aa63358a5e030610d33f5a1eef5d48ba22881a1ddd3ede1d8a9f3ed88baf"}},{"id":"f7131a46c19f7dcf4fb45ca6f979e621a462471c0cdf0df741bc8af13a706921","quote":"Most of our legacy healthcare facilities are leased to single tenants under triple-net leases. Our portfolio also contains some multi-tenant properties with gross lease or modified gross lease structures. In addition, we own SHOP communities from which we derive revenue from resident agreements. As of June 30, 2026, we also had an interest in four unconsolidated joint ventures that own or are developing healthcare and active adult facilities.","context":"We also intend to utilize our experience and knowledge of inpatient rehabilitation facilities and outpatient medical real estate to manage our existing joint ventures and to evaluate healthcare real estate opportunities that complement our seniors housing strategy.","section":"Business Overview and Strategy","block":449,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-093347","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-10","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001533615","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1533615/000110465926093347/xrn-20260630x10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/94b4aa63358a5e030610d33f5a1eef5d48ba22881a1ddd3ede1d8a9f3ed88baf.bin","sha256":"94b4aa63358a5e030610d33f5a1eef5d48ba22881a1ddd3ede1d8a9f3ed88baf"}},{"id":"83bcbbdd9d70abe543cab1113531f6cca20e0926acc0c703c16bd65becef3203","quote":"As of June 30, 2026, we had gross investments of approximately $1.6 billion in real estate, consisting of 182 healthcare facilities, primarily outpatient medical facilities, with an aggregate of approximately 4.6 million leasable square feet, and 2 SHOP communities, with an aggregate of 292 homes. This data does not include amounts for properties held in our unconsolidated joint ventures.","context":"Our Properties","section":"Business Overview and Strategy","block":451,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-093347","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-10","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001533615","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1533615/000110465926093347/xrn-20260630x10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/94b4aa63358a5e030610d33f5a1eef5d48ba22881a1ddd3ede1d8a9f3ed88baf.bin","sha256":"94b4aa63358a5e030610d33f5a1eef5d48ba22881a1ddd3ede1d8a9f3ed88baf"}},{"id":"25ed02ebad74021b89a5e5b3ec190fd3c47e4a67845115df952cb1717928c552","quote":"On June 1, 2026, the Company completed the acquisition of The Landing Alexandria (the “Landing”), a 163-home, luxury seniors housing community located in Alexandria, Virginia, from affiliates of Silverstone Senior Living (“SSL”) for a purchase price of approximately $130 million. The Landing has operated since May 2022 and offers independent living, assisted living and memory care.","context":"Acquired Properties","section":"Business Overview and Strategy","block":454,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-093347","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-10","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001533615","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1533615/000110465926093347/xrn-20260630x10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/94b4aa63358a5e030610d33f5a1eef5d48ba22881a1ddd3ede1d8a9f3ed88baf.bin","sha256":"94b4aa63358a5e030610d33f5a1eef5d48ba22881a1ddd3ede1d8a9f3ed88baf"}},{"id":"e80ef293ca5e3265e8623a8160895d3dff2b3279ab192a4692a21f5500c03001","quote":"On June 1, 2026, the Company completed the acquisition of The Riviera at Alexandria (the “Riviera”), a 129-home, luxury seniors housing community located in Alexandria, Virginia, from affiliates of SSL for a purchase price of approximately $119 million. The Riviera is a newly developed independent living community that opened in March 2026 and remains in lease-up.","context":"On June 1, 2026, the Company completed the acquisition of The Landing Alexandria (the “Landing”), a 163-home, luxury seniors housing community located in Alexandria, Virginia, from affiliates of Silverstone Senior Living (“SSL”) for a purchase price of approximately $130 million. The Landing has operated since May 2022 and offers independent living, assisted living and memory care.","section":"Business Overview and Strategy","block":455,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-093347","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-10","reportDate":"2026-0